.TH SUKUT 1 "October 2026" "Sukut 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sukut \- remove music from your computer's audio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sukut
.br
.B sukut \-\-tray
.br
.B sukut \-\-restore\-audio
.br
.B sukut \-\-phone
.IR command " [" \-\-serial " " SERIAL ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sukut
opens Sukut's window. Sukut removes music from what the computer plays while
keeping speech and other sounds, using its own PipeWire output. Its background
part,
.BR sukut\-host ,
starts with the window, owns the audio engine and the tray icon, and keeps
running in the tray when the window is closed (if Close to tray is on).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Start Sukut in the tray without opening the window. The optional
"Start with system" setting uses this.
.TP
.B \-\-restore\-audio
Undo audio routing left behind if Sukut was stopped abnormally: the default
output (only if it still names Sukut's output) and redirected app streams.
Sukut must not be running.
.TP
.BI \-\-phone " command"
Run a phone tool from the terminal, as on the Phone page: \fBdevices\fR,
\fBinspect\fR, \fBstatus\fR, \fBinstall\fR, \fBupdate\fR, \fBsetup\fR,
\fBopen\fR, \fBactivate\fR, \fBdeactivate\fR or \fBallow\-usb\fR. Uses \fBadb\fR(1);
\fBallow\-usb\fR asks for administrator permission through \fBpkexec\fR(1).
.TP
.BI \-\-serial " SERIAL"
With \fB\-\-phone\fR, the phone to use when more than one is connected.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sukut/settings.json
Settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/sukut/routing.json
The routing journal used to restore audio.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR adb (1),
.BR pipewire (1),
.BR wpctl (1)
